  "details": "Currently, you can change the height of your avatar via the avatar height dial in your quick menu. This dial has a range of 0.20m to 5m. \n\nIt would be nice if the range of this could be reduced by the user. \n\nPersonally I'm only ever interested in adjusting my height between like 1 and 1.88 meters. While having the option to go below or above that is nice from time to time, this means most of the dial's range is allocated to measurements I'll barely or never use. \n\nThe issue that I run into with this large range, is that when using VR controllers, the small range which I do like to use is really hard to dial in (pun absolutely intended). Because of how imprecise the dial is to control with joysticks, the stepping within this small range is really large, making it close to impossible to pick certain heights. This gets even worse around the snap point of the avatar's default height, as the distance between the snapping point and the first allowed value that are far away enough from that point to not snap, is quite substantial on this 0.2-5m scale.\n\nThis issue would be solved for me if I could somehow configure VRChat to reduce the range on the dial.",
